  SuitSprite: {fileID: 0}
  CardStory: "Something itches in the back of Spades2 head. He felt it today in the
    mess hall, a vague sense of wrongness. Spades2 hesitates. Nothing was wrong,
    was it? Yes, it was. People are supposed to blink. Spades2 blinks, of course.
    \n\nHe has blinked today, multiple times. Long day, hasn\u2019t it been? I suppose
    that\u2019s true. I should make sure. Spades2 asks Clubs2, who sits in front
    of me, chewing while we chat. She blinks and opens her eyes wide at my question.
    She laughs, I don\u2019t know her expression. \r\n\r\nSpades2 enjoys his talks
    with Clubs2. She always knows what to say. She tells me about her day around
    a mouthful of stew. I learn a lot from Clubs2. \r\n\r\nWhen they leave the mess
    hall together, Spades2 remembers to blink. Blinking is important. Clubs2 stops
    chewing, of course. Chewing is for when you\u2019re in the mess hall."
